<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy | Adorable"
  description="How Adorable AB processes personal data on adorable.se and when you contact us."
  updated="2 September 2026"
  lang="en"
  alternatePath="/privacy"
>
  <p>This policy describes how Adorable AB processes personal data when you visit adorable.se, send a message or express interest in the newsletter.</p>

  <h2>Data controller</h2>
  <p>Adorable AB, Swedish organisation number 559095-2122, is the data controller. Contact <a href="mailto:peter@adorable.se">peter@adorable.se</a> with questions or to exercise your rights.</p>

  <h2>Data we process</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact:</strong> name, email address, company, selected interest and your message.</li>
    <li><strong>Website:</strong> basic technical information and anonymised usage statistics.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> the email address you choose to pass to Substack's subscription page.</li>
    <li><strong>Client relationship:</strong> contact, contract and invoicing information needed to deliver and administer an engagement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Purposes and legal bases</h2>
  <p>Contact data is used to answer enquiries, prepare a possible engagement and communicate in an existing client relationship. Depending on the situation, processing is based on steps before a contract, performance of a contract, a legal obligation or Adorable's legitimate interest in operating and developing the business.</p>
  <p>Newsletter subscriptions are handled by Substack after you continue to and complete registration on its service. Any consent and unsubscribe choices are managed there.</p>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> hosts and delivers the website and may process technical traffic and security information.</li>
    <li><strong>Umami Cloud</strong> provides website statistics. It is configured without cookies and Umami describes the service as not automatically collecting personal data.</li>
    <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong> processes contact-form data and forwards it to Adorable. According to its documentation, processing uses US infrastructure and server logs may be kept for a limited period.</li>
    <li><strong>Substack</strong> provides the newsletter. Once you continue to Substack, it processes data under its own privacy policy.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Adorable does not sell personal data. Data is shared only when needed for these purposes, to comply with law or to protect legal interests.</p>

  <h2>Transfers outside the EU/EEA</h2>
  <p>Some providers may process data outside the EU/EEA. Where GDPR applies, Adorable will use an applicable transfer mechanism, such as an adequacy decision or standard contractual clauses.</p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>Data is not kept longer than needed for its purpose. A routine enquiry is deleted or anonymised when it is no longer needed. Records connected to a contract, accounting or a legal obligation may need to be retained for longer.</p>

  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>Adorable does not use advertising cookies on the website. Umami analytics is cookieless. External services you visit through a link apply their own choices and policies.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Where the conditions are met, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction or portability and object to processing. Contact <a href="mailto:peter@adorable.se">peter@adorable.se</a>. You may also lodge a complaint with the <a href="https://www.imy.se/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection, IMY</a>.</p>

  <h2>Provider policies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vercel Privacy Notice</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://umami.is/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Umami Privacy Policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://docs.web3forms.com/getting-started/faq" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Web3Forms GDPR and privacy information</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://substack.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Substack Privacy Policy</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>This policy is updated when website data processing or applicable requirements change. The current date is shown above.</p>
</LegalPage>
